# Django Fixtures Standard

When creating or modifying Django fixtures in this project, you MUST follow the Django Fixtures Standard. This ensures consistency, predictability, and reliable fixture loading.

## Core Requirements

### 1. Directory Organization (REQUIRED)

- Organize fixtures by field name: `<app>/fixtures/<field_name>/`
- Each field gets its own directory
- Structure:

  ```text
  <app>/fixtures/
  ├── <field_name>/
  │   ├── coding.yaml
  │   └── codeable_concept.yaml (if needed)
  ```

### 2. Fixture File Format (REQUIRED)

**File Header (REQUIRED):**

Every fixture file MUST start with a header comment containing:
- Field name description
- CodeSystem URL
- Version (if available)

**Entry Comments (REQUIRED):**

Each fixture entry MUST have a comment above it describing the code/entry.

**Coding Fixture:**

```yaml
# <Field Name> Coding fixtures
# CodeSystem: <code-system-url>
# Version: <version>

# <Code Display Name>
- model: fhir.coding
  pk: <explicit-uuid>
  fields:
    created_at: <iso-timestamp>
    updated_at: <iso-timestamp>
    system: <code-system-url>
    version: <version>
    code: <code-value>
    display: <human-readable-display>
    user_selected: false
```

**Note:** The `version` field MUST use the same version value specified in the file header comment. Do NOT use `null` unless the CodeSystem truly has no version.

**CodeableConcept Fixture:**

```yaml
# <Field Name> CodeableConcept fixtures
# CodeSystem: <code-system-url>
# Version: <version>

# <Code Display Name>
- model: fhir.codeableconcept
  pk: <explicit-uuid>
  fields:
    created_at: <iso-timestamp>
    updated_at: <iso-timestamp>
    text: <full-definition-text>
    coding:
      - <coding-pk-1>
      - <coding-pk-2>
```

### 3. Required Fields (MANDATORY)

**UUIDs:**

- MUST use explicit UUIDs (never `pk: null`)
- Use UUID v4 format: `33e2795c-1ebf-4929-815c-4b4d6bb367e6`
- Required for referencing in ManyToMany relationships

**Timestamps:**

- MUST include `created_at` and `updated_at` in ALL fixtures
- Use ISO 8601 format: `2025-03-16T00:00:00Z`
- BaseModel auto fields don't work in fixtures

**System URLs:**

- MUST match registered CodeSystem URLs exactly
- Example: `http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/allergyintolerance-clinical`

**Text Field (CodeableConcept):**

- Use full definition text (not just display name)
- Match FHIR resource definitions

### 4. Load Order (CRITICAL)

**Dependencies MUST be loaded before dependents:**

1. Load Coding fixtures first
2. Then load CodeableConcept fixtures (which reference Coding)

**Loading Commands:**

```bash
# Load Coding first
python manage.py loaddata <app>/fixtures/<field>/coding

# Then load CodeableConcept
python manage.py loaddata <app>/fixtures/<field>/coding <app>/fixtures/<field>/codeable_concept
```

### 5. Field Type Patterns

**ForeignKey to CodeableConcept:**

- Create `coding.yaml` with all codes
- Create `codeable_concept.yaml` with CodeableConcept instances
- Each CodeableConcept references Coding UUIDs

**ManyToMany to Coding:**

- Create `coding.yaml` with all codes
- No CodeableConcept fixture needed

**ForeignKey to Coding:**

- Create `coding.yaml` with all codes
- No CodeableConcept fixture needed

### 6. ManyToMany Relationships

- Set ManyToMany fields directly in fixtures
- List related object PKs under the field name
- Example: List Coding PKs under `coding` field in CodeableConcept fixtures

### 7. Adding New Codes

1. Open appropriate `coding.yaml` file
2. Add new entry with explicit UUID
3. Ensure `system` URL matches field's code system
4. Set `created_at` and `updated_at` timestamps
5. If using CodeableConcept, add/update CodeableConcept fixture
6. Load fixtures in order: Coding first, then CodeableConcept

### 8. Code System Documentation

Document code systems for each field:

| Field | Code System URL | Type | Fixture Files |
|-------|----------------|------|---------------|
| `<field>` | `<url>` | ForeignKey to CodeableConcept | `coding.yaml`, `codeable_concept.yaml` |
| `<field>` | `<url>` | ManyToMany to Coding | `coding.yaml` |
| `<field>` | `<url>` | ForeignKey to Coding | `coding.yaml` |

## Complete Example

**Model Field:**

```python
clinical_status = models.ForeignKey(
    "fhir.CodeableConcept",
    on_delete=models.SET_NULL,
    null=True,
    blank=True,
    related_name="model_name_clinical_status",
    help_text=_("Clinical status: active | inactive | resolved"),
)
```

**Fixture Structure:**

```text
fixtures/
└── clinical_status/
    ├── coding.yaml
    └── codeable_concept.yaml
```

**coding.yaml:**

```yaml
# Clinical Status Coding fixtures
# CodeSystem: http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/allergyintolerance-clinical
# Version: 0.5.0

# Active
- model: fhir.coding
  pk: 33e2795c-1ebf-4929-815c-4b4d6bb367e6
  fields:
    created_at: 2025-03-16T00:00:00Z
    updated_at: 2025-03-16T00:00:00Z
    system: http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/allergyintolerance-clinical
    version: 0.5.0
    code: active
    display: Active
    user_selected: false
```

**codeable_concept.yaml:**

```yaml
# Clinical Status CodeableConcept fixtures
# CodeSystem: http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/allergyintolerance-clinical
# Version: 0.5.0

# Active
- model: fhir.codeableconcept
  pk: a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890
  fields:
    created_at: 2025-03-16T00:00:00Z
    updated_at: 2025-03-16T00:00:00Z
    text: The subject is currently experiencing, or is at risk of, a reaction to the identified substance.
    coding:
      - 33e2795c-1ebf-4929-815c-4b4d6bb367e6
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ **Using `pk: null`** - Always use explicit UUIDs
❌ **Missing timestamps** - Always include `created_at` and `updated_at`
❌ **Wrong load order** - Load Coding before CodeableConcept
❌ **System URL mismatch** - Verify URLs match FHIR terminology servers
❌ **Short text** - Use full definition text, not just display name
❌ **Missing UUIDs in references** - All Coding UUIDs must exist before referencing
❌ **Missing file header** - Always include CodeSystem and Version in header comments
❌ **Missing entry comments** - Always add a comment above each entry describing the code
❌ **Load order comments in files** - Do NOT include load order comments in fixture files (documented in this standard)
❌ **Using `version: null`** - Always use the version from the file header comment unless the CodeSystem truly has no version

## Checklist

When creating fixtures, ensure:

- [ ] Directory structure follows field-based organization
- [ ] File header includes CodeSystem and Version comments
- [ ] Each entry has a descriptive comment above it
- [ ] All fixtures use explicit UUIDs (not `pk: null`)
- [ ] All fixtures include `created_at` and `updated_at` timestamps
- [ ] System URLs match registered CodeSystem URLs
- [ ] Version field uses the version from the file header comment (not `null`)
- [ ] Coding fixtures are created before CodeableConcept fixtures
- [ ] CodeableConcept fixtures reference existing Coding UUIDs
- [ ] Text fields use full definition text
- [ ] Load order is documented and tested

